ested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Map AC7 (signed-read-set), AC8 (subprocess spy), and AC9 (schema/docs) to explicit test files and add them to the Verification pytest command (or state where each check runs).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8714,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Verification runs: test_terraform_index.py test_terraform_tools.py test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py test_core_optionality.py test_capabilities.py","AC7 'Signed-read-set tests observe all parsed files/patterns, then add a sibling .tf and observe freshness change.'","AC8 'A subprocess spy observes no Terraform, OpenTofu, provider, tfparse, TFLint, Trivy...'","AC9 'Schema tests validate evidence/receipt objects; docs/grounding.md documents...'"],"finding":"Several acceptance criteria have no matching test file in the Verification pytest command, leaving their proving commands unstated: AC7 (signed-read-set freshness), AC8 (subprocess spy observing no executable), and AC9 (schema validation + docs/grounding.md).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f944b56bb6ec8d409","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification section vs Acceptance Criteria AC7/AC8/AC9","norm_id":"n7f63ab9853d64141","priority":0.0786,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor runs the Verification command, sees green, but the no-executable spy and schema tests were never invoked."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add the freshness/read-set test, the subprocess-spy test, and a schema-validation test file to the Verification command, e.g. append tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_no_exec.py and tests/unit/schemas/test_terraform_grounding_receipt.py.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the receipt config_digest/result_digest routes through rebar._store.canonical (content_hash/canonical_bytes) rather than a new inline json.dumps, since the specified form is byte-identical to that declared single seam.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7025,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["src/rebar/_store/canonical.py docstring: 'the one true canonical-JSON/hash home ... the single seam for the other \"sorted-key compact JSON (+ sha256)\" sites that had each reimplemented it inline'; canonical_str uses json.dumps(doc, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\", \":\"), sort_keys=True) and content_hash returns sha256 of those bytes — identical to the plan's config/result digest spec.","The module explicitly warns that a caller that diverges should do so 'explicitly (a named param with a cited consumer) rather than via a silent copy'.","The snapshot/module digest (length-prefixed paths + raw bytes) is a di